/**
 * GENERATED — do not edit by hand.
 *   python3 -I scripts/build-recorded-dataset.py \
 *       data/hs-audits-2025Q4-2026Q1.json data/hs-audits-2026Q3.json \
 *       --observations data/observations-2025Q4-2026Q3.json \
 *       --observations-out src/lib/ehss/recorded-observations.ts \
 *       > src/lib/ehss/recorded.ts
 *
 * The real Health & Safety audits for Q4 2025, Q1 2026 and Q3 2026, as read
 * from HS_AUDIT_FINDINGS.xlsx and the AL FAHD (272) quarterly review
 * workbook. This is the app's dataset: there is no demo data.
 *
 * Contractors are INITIALS + THE LAST THREE DIGITS OF THE WORK ORDER, which
 * is all the app ever sees. It keeps the dataset unidentifying, and it
 * settles the source file's three spellings of SIBS by construction.
 *
 * Each findings audit carries the checklist's 15 AREA scores as raw points.
 * The findings sheets record a narrative per question and no
 * machine-readable answer, so those audits have an empty `responses`. The
 * one review workbook (af272-2026-Q3) records an answer per question and
 * carries them, with the causes of each gap read from its observations
 * (recorded-observations.ts; see Q3_REFERENCES in the build script), and
 * NO area points: its printed C1
 * "possible" disagrees with its own answers, so it is scored from the
 * answers alone.
 * `possible` varies between audits because N/A questions drop out of it,
 * which is the workbook's own rule.
 *
 * `reportedTotal` is the total the sheet stated. It disagrees with the
 * sheet's own points in 7 of 20 audits (see docs/IMPORT-2025Q4-2026Q1.md);
 * the app scores the points and shows the stated figure beside it rather
 * than quietly picking one.
 */

